MAKE(1)                       User Commands

NAME
    make - maintain program dependencies

SYNOPSIS
    make [--posix] [-C path] [-f makefile] [-j num] [-x pragma]
         [-ehiknpqrsSt] [macro[:[:[:]]]=value ...] [target ...]

DESCRIPTION
    Reads the rules in makefile (Makefile or makefile by default, - for
    standard input) and rebuilds every named target whose prerequisites are
    newer than it, running the commands of the rule with /bin/sh. This is
    pdpmake, the public domain make of Ron Yorston, which implements the
    make of POSIX 2024 with these extensions: double colon rules, ifdef,
    ifndef, ifeq, ifneq, else and endif, archive members lib.a(member.o),
    := assignments, chained inference rules, wildcards in target rules,
    a backslash escaping #,     $< and $* in target rules, -C directory,
    and macros and targets mixed on the command line. .POSIX as the first
    target, the --posix option or the environment variable
    PDPMAKE_POSIXLY_CORRECT disable the extensions.

    -e lets the environment override makefile macros, -f names the
    makefile (repeatable), -i ignores command errors, -k continues with
    other targets after an error, -n prints commands without running them,
    -p prints the macros and rules, -q reports with the exit status whether
    the targets are current, -r drops the built-in rules, -s runs silently,
    -S stops at the first error (the default), -t touches the targets
    instead of building them, -C changes to the directory first, -j is
    accepted and ignored, -h prints the usage.

SEE ALSO
    sh(1), touch(1), index(7)
